                <invention-title lang="de">PLANUNG VON ANWENDUNGSVERZÖGERUNGEN</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">PROGRAMMATION DE RETARD D'APPLICATION</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">SCHEDULING APPLICATION DELAY</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>Certain aspects of the present disclosure provide techniques for managing scheduling of wireless communications. A method that may be performed by a user equipment (UE) includes receiving, from a base station, one or more configurations indicating a plurality of minimum scheduling offset values; receiving, from the base station via a first bandwidth part, BWP, within a first carrier, a signal indicating one of the minimum scheduling offset values as an updated value to be used for communications with the base station and indicating to communicate with the base station via a second BWP within a second carrier that is different from the first carrier; determining a delay based on numerologies of the first BWP and the second BWP; and communicating with the base station via the second BWP using the updated value based on expiration of the delay.</p>
            </abstract>
